<LegalPage eyebrow="Privacy" title="Privacy Policy" description="What Vector stores locally, what billing requires, and what connected providers receive.">
  <section><h2>Local and cloud workspaces</h2><p>Vector's desktop workspace is designed to keep repositories, local sessions, preferences, and checkpoints on your computer. If you launch a Cloud Agent or agent team, the repository and task context you select are copied into an isolated cloud workspace so that the run can continue while your computer is offline. Cloud workspace files, logs, diffs, screenshots, usage, and messages are retained until you remove the workspace or Vector applies its published retention policy.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Accounts and platform data</h2><p>Vector accounts use Supabase Auth. Vector stores your account identifier, email, display profile, subscription entitlement, API-key hashes and settings, Cloud Agent metadata, API workbench collections and history, usage records, and configured tool metadata. API secrets are shown once and stored as one-way hashes. Saved connection credentials and API environment values are encrypted at rest with a server-managed application key.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Cloud execution</h2><p>Vector uses Vercel infrastructure for the website, server functions, scheduled reconciliation, and isolated Cloud Agent sandboxes. Selected repository content, prompts, command output, and tool results may be processed there. Model requests made by Cloud Agents can pass through Vercel AI Gateway to the model provider selected for the run. Vector does not place its master model credential inside customer-controlled sandboxes.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Model and tool providers</h2><p>Prompts, selected files, tool results, or other context may be sent to the model and integration providers you choose. Their privacy policies apply. Vector does not centrally store your model API keys as part of the license service.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Billing and license data</h2><p>Stripe processes payment details. Vector receives and stores the billing email, Stripe customer and subscription identifiers, subscription status, renewal state, license metadata, a hashed activation token, a one-way device identifier, device name/platform, and recent verification timestamps. Vector does not receive your full card number.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Purchase email</h2><p>Resend delivers the purchase confirmation and license key. The message contains your billing email, license key, expiration date, and purchase link. Resend processes that delivery under its own privacy terms.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Diagnostics</h2><p>Some Vector builds may use Sentry for crash diagnostics. Diagnostic reports can include application version, operating system, stack traces, and technical state. Vector does not intentionally attach repository files to crash reports.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Security and retention</h2><p>Activation tokens are stored locally in a restricted application file. Server-side records store hashes rather than plaintext activation tokens. Billing, account, API, cloud-run, and license records are retained as needed to provide access, recover workspaces, prevent abuse, resolve disputes, and satisfy legal obligations. Deleting an isolated workspace removes its provider sandbox before Vector removes the database record.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You can disconnect providers, remove local data, cancel renewal, and deactivate a computer from Vector. For billing or privacy requests, contact <a href="mailto:contact.astr0gpt@gmail.com">contact.astr0gpt@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
</LegalPage>
